# Grist — the keys stored in secrets.sops.json, one value each (`sopsgen
# apply` fills generated ones, `sopsedit` the rest). Values built from other
# secrets live in env.nix. Key set must match secrets.sops.json and
# tests/fixtures/stacks/grist.sops.json.

# Sessions
# Signs the session cookie. Unset, Grist falls back to a default that is
# hard-coded in its public source, and every cookie becomes forgeable.
# Rotating logs everyone out and nothing more. openssl rand -hex 32
GRIST_SESSION_SECRET=changeme_hex32

# Break-glass
# The install admin's login at /boot: this key plus GRIST_ADMIN_EMAIL, no
# Authentik in the loop (the server still needs OIDC discovery to start).
# Grist prints it to the container log at every start. Never set it empty —
# an empty key matches an empty submission. openssl rand -hex 32
GRIST_BOOT_KEY=changeme_hex32
